  real:'The exam room is also where grandpa gets his knee checked and where new babies are weighed — it is the doctor’s office, and its door opens for everyone.',
  play:'Crumple Choir: everyone gets a sheet of paper; the conductor points and the paper crinkles loud or soft. The sound that startles in a quiet clinic becomes an instrument here — mastered, owned, funny.',
  safety:'The exam bed is high — one hand on the child at all times in the real room, no exceptions, teddy positioned away from the edge. Say it the same way at home: "teddy sits in the middle."',
